        </Pagination>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>The cross-linking relation between the evidence of outside living tick populations and specific vegetation units allows for efficiently using the vegetation maps, and more especially the medium scale maps. Ixodes ricinus is referred to here as an example. The limitations of this data derived from such maps are evaluated by the authors. They suggest some means aiding in improving their efficiency through the knowledge of the ecological variables playing a role in the species settlement.</AbstractText>
