        <ArticleTitle>Mucocutaneous lymph node syndrome with coronary artery aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
        <Pagination>
          <MedlinePgn>596-8</MedlinePgn>
        </Pagination>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>A white North American girl with clinical features of the mucocutaneous lymph node syndrome had a myocardial infarct and angiographic evidence of a coronary artery aneurysm and mitral regurgitation. The mucocutaneous lymph node syndrome has been extensively diagnosed in Japan in recent years. It appears to be a distinct entity, although not precisely separated from polyarteritis nodosa in childhood. The condition may be more common than previously realized.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
